From 2e62eace324d28b2db5e3727dce04b6a73a41a27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:53:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(docs): fail the prose job when a recorded count has
 drifted

The job already runs Vale over the gated set. It now also runs
ts/scripts/vale-counts.cjs, which compares every number .vale.ini and
docs/STYLE-GUIDE.md record against that run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0112y49CCjc7bpiu6GsCKWc4
---
 .github/workflows/docs.yml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/docs.yml b/.github/workflows/docs.yml
index 0e0afac..5b8d32f 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/docs.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/docs.yml
@@ -80,6 +80,13 @@ jobs:
       - name: Prose gate
         run: vale --minAlertLevel=error $(node ts/scripts/gated-docs.cjs)
 
+      # .vale.ini justifies every demoted rule with the number of alerts
+      # it produced here, and docs/STYLE-GUIDE.md repeats the total. Both
+      # were written by hand and were out by a factor of two before
+      # anything compared them to a run. This step does.
+      - name: Recorded alert counts
+        run: node ts/scripts/vale-counts.cjs
+
       # Warnings and suggestions are reported for the author to read and
       # do not block; see the demotion notes in .vale.ini for what sits
       # at which level and why.
-- 
